# NestJS TypeORM Entity Generation

When creating or updating an entity file, follow this exact structure. Do not inspect other files for style decisions.

## Required pattern

- Use `import {BaseModel} from 'nestjs-typeorm-shared'`.
- Keep all TypeORM imports from `typeorm` in one grouped import.
- Add `@Entity({ name: '<table_name>' })`. Table name should be plural in snake case.
- Entity class must extend `BaseModel`.
- Use explicit decorators for every field (`@PrimaryColumn`, `@Column`, `@ManyToOne`, `@OneToMany`, `@JoinColumn`).
- For FK scalar fields, define `@Column({ foreignKeyConstraintName: 'FK_...' })` and matching `@JoinColumn` on relation.
- Add `@Injectable()` repository in the same file.
- Repository must extend `Repository<EntityName>`, call `super(EntityName, dataSource.createEntityManager())`, and override `createQueryBuilder` to return typed query-builder.
- Primary column is increment for reference/enum tables and uuid v7 (`@PrimaryColumn({ type: 'uuid', default: () => UUIDV7_FUNC })`) for other.

## Golden example (copy this shape)

```typescript
import {BaseModel} from 'nestjs-typeorm-shared'
import { Injectable } from '@nestjs/common'
import {
  Entity,
  Repository,
  DataSource,
  QueryRunner,
  PrimaryColumn,
  Column,
  OneToMany,
  ManyToOne,
  JoinColumn,
} from 'typeorm'
import { ExampleQueryBuilder } from '../query-builders/example.qb'
import { ForeignEntity } from '@modules/foreign/entities/foreign.entity'
import { ChildEntity } from '@modules/child/entities/child.entity'

@Entity({ name: 'example_entities' })
export class ExampleEntity extends BaseModel {
  @PrimaryColumn({ generated: 'increment', generatedIdentity: 'BY DEFAULT' })
  <example_entity>_id: number

  @Column()
  <example_entity>_name: string

  @Column({ nullable: true, foreignKeyConstraintName: 'FK_foreign_id' })
  foreign_id?: number

  @ManyToOne(() => ForeignEntity, (parent) => parent.examples, {
    onUpdate: 'CASCADE',
    onDelete: 'SET NULL',
  })
  @JoinColumn({
    name: 'foreign_id',
    referencedColumnName: 'foreign_id',
    foreignKeyConstraintName: 'FK_foreign_id',
  })
  foreign?: ForeignEntity

  @OneToMany(() => ChildEntity, (child) => child.example)
  children?: ChildEntity[]
}

@Injectable()
export class ExampleEntityRepository extends Repository<ExampleEntity> {
  constructor(private dataSource: DataSource) {
    super(ExampleEntity, dataSource.createEntityManager())
  }

  override createQueryBuilder(alias?: string, queryRunner?: QueryRunner): ExampleQueryBuilder {
    const queryBuilder = super.createQueryBuilder(alias, queryRunner)
    return new ExampleQueryBuilder(queryBuilder)
  }
}
```
